    "created_at": "2017-05-30T12:16:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-30T12:16:54Z",
    "body": "So we need to figure out what the setter should do also to fix this.\r\n\r\nhttp://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=5213\r\n\r\n<dl>\r\n<dt>EdgeHTML\r\n<dd>\r\n\r\n```\r\nlog: 1000: 1000\r\nlog: 1001: Error: Invalid argument.\r\nlog: 2147483647: Error: Invalid argument.\r\nlog: 2147483648: Error: Invalid argument.\r\nlog: 2147483650: Error: Invalid argument.\r\nlog: 4294967300: 4\r\n```\r\n\r\n<dt>Gecko & WebKit\r\n<dd>\r\n\r\n```\r\nlog: 1000: 1000\r\nlog: 1001: 1001\r\nlog: 2147483647: 2147483647\r\nlog: 2147483648: 1\r\nlog: 2147483650: 1\r\nlog: 4294967300: 4\r\n```\r\n\r\n<dt>Chromium\r\n<dd>\r\n\r\n```\r\nlog: 1000: 1000\r\nlog: 1001: 1001\r\nlog: 2147483647: 2147483647\r\nlog: 2147483648: 0\r\nlog: 2147483650: 0\r\nlog: 4294967300: 4\r\n```\r\n\r\n</dl>\r\n\r\nThe [spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#limited-to-only-non-negative-numbers-greater-than-zero-with-fallback) is like Gecko & WebKit I believe. The only other reflecting attributes using the \"with fallback\" thing in the spec are [textarea cols and rows](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-textarea-cols).\r\n\r\nGiven the lack of interop and the fact that EdgeHTML throws, it seems possible to switch to \"[clamped to the range](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#clamped-to-the-range)\", like colSpan/rowSpan.",
